  ],
  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "To medium 29 add 1% NaCl"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Fill 10x 46ml in 100 ml screw-cap bottles. Bubble with N2/CO2and autoclave 121°C 15 min."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "(For marine or estuarine isolates add 100.0 g NaCl to this solution and increase the MgSO4x 7 H2O to 15.0 g)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "Prepare in a screw-cap bottle, bubble with N2 to replace air, close tightly and autoclave."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": "Bubble with CO2 and filter sterilize into sterile, gas-tight, 100 ml screw-cap bottle."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 15,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 17,
      "comment": "Autoclave in a cotton-stoppered Erlenmeyer flask withan outlet tube for medium, connected to a glass outlet atthe bottom of the vessel and has, at the other end, a silicon rubber tube with a pinch cock and a bell for aseptic dispensing of the medium into bottles."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": "Cool to room temperature under an atmosphere of N2/CO2in an ice bath."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 19,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 21,
      "comment": "Filter sterilize into sterile, gas-tight, 100 ml screw-cap bottle."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 22,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 24,
      "comment": "Filter sterilized"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 25,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 27,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 28,
      "comment": "Mix solution D, C and E. Bubble with CO2in an ice bath under sterile conditions. Fill 50 ml in each bottle of solution A. Before using add 4 ml solution B and 0.1 ml solution F."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 29,
      "comment": "Adjust the pH with filter-sterilised 1M Na2CO3to 6.8 -7.1."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 30,
      "comment": "Fill in sterile, N2gassed screw-cap tubes under N2gas."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 31,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 32,
      "comment": "During the first 24 h, the iron of the medium precipitates in the form of black flocks. No other sediment should arise in the otherwise clear medium. Feed periodically with neutralized 3% solution of sodium sulfide to replenish sulfide and with other supplement solutions (see Ref. 3365)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 33,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 35,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 36,
      "comment": "The sulfide solution is prepared in a 250 ml screw-capped bottle with a butyl rubber septum and a magnetic stirrer. The solution is bubbled with nitrogen gas, closed and autoclaved for 15 min. at 121°C. After cooling to room temperaturethe pH is adjusted to about 7.0 by adding of sterile 2 N H2SO4drop-wise with a syringe without opening the bottle."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 37,
      "comment": "Appearance of a yellow colour indicatesthe drop of pH to about 8. The solution should be stirred continuously to avoid precipitation of elemental sulfur. The final solution should be clear and is yellow in colour."
    }
  ]
}